# Counter-example: the conservative retreat. Fetch, throw your rewrite away,
# and take whatever origin has.
#
# Nothing is lost and nothing is gained: their test is back, and so are the
# two commits you squashed. It is the right instinct in a real emergency and
# it is not an answer to the task, which was to publish the tidied-up branch.

git fetch origin
git reset --hard origin/feature/search-ui
git log --oneline --decorate --all
